/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  curate21_vp_diEthylCarbonate -- the vapour pressure of diEthylCarbonate, REFITTED to
  measurements (DEV.md 4c C281 step 2).  Written by `bin/choupo-curate vp
  diEthylCarbonate`; everything above the RESULT paragraph is the DECLARATION, committed
  before any fit ran, so it can be read against the result.

  WHY.  The catalogue record carried `vaporPressure { model AmbroseWalton; }`,
  a corresponding-states ESTIMATE from Tc, Pc and omega that never reads the
  record's own Tb (C279 measured a median 19.6 % AAD over the 25 such records
  with archive data).  Here a three-parameter Antoine is fitted to ONE
  laboratory and held out on ANOTHER that shares no author with it.

  STUDIES (one per article, extracted by `choupo-thermoml extract-vp`; ranked
  by points, ties by DOI):
      10.1016/j.jct.2008.02.012        44 pts  273.1-315.2 K  Kozlova; Emel'yanenko; Georgieva; Verevkin et al.
      10.1021/acs.jced.7b00295         42 pts  238.15-296.15 K  Pokorny; Stejfa; Fulem; Cervinka et al.
      10.1021/je200784y                33 pts  354.68-399.27 K  Marrufo; Loras; Lladosa
      10.1021/je800984q                21 pts  343.77-398.28 K  Xing; Fang; Li; Guo et al.
      10.1016/j.jct.2014.07.004        17 pts  277.96-353.15 K  Dougassa; Jacquemin; Ouatani; Tessier et al.
      10.1021/acs.jced.7b00236         10 pts  303.15-323.15 K  Anugraha; Altway; Wibawa
  SET ASIDE BY NAME:
      10.1016/j.fluid.2012.11.026: 2 pressure point(s), fewer than 5
      10.1016/j.jct.2015.07.024: 3 pressure point(s), fewer than 5
      10.1021/acs.jced.5b00064: 1 pressure point(s), fewer than 5
      10.1021/acs.jced.6b00085: 1 pressure point(s), fewer than 5
      10.1021/acs.jced.9b00068: 1 pressure point(s), fewer than 5
      10.1021/acs.jced.9b00430: 1 pressure point(s), fewer than 5
      10.1021/je049544x: 1 pressure point(s), fewer than 5

  PARTITION (the C16 rule, declared): FIT = the study with the most points,
  doi 10.1016/j.jct.2008.02.012 (44 pts, 273.1-315.2 K); HELD OUT =
  the next largest sharing no author with it, doi 10.1021/acs.jced.7b00295 (42 pts,
  238.15-296.15 K).

  BAND: maxAAD 2.0 % (declared before the fit by bin/choupo-curate vp (C281 step 2): the held-out study's own stated relative expanded uncertainty U95(P)/P, AVERAGED over its 42 points (1.29 to 3.99 %, mean 1.947 %), rounded UP to two significant figures -- a mean held against the held-out AAD, which is a mean).

  NORMAL BOILING POINT: the record's Tb 399.95 K lies OUTSIDE the measured span 238.15-315.2 K: the fitted Antoine's own normal boiling point (P = 101.325 kPa) must lie within 2 K of it, or the fit is NOT promoted (an extrapolation that misses the record's own boiling point).

  NO MEASURED POINT IS IN THIS TREE: constant/archiveDatasets declares both
  series by DOI, NIST URL and sha256; `bin/choupo-curate fetch` regenerates
  them into constant/archiveExtracts/ (gitignored).

  RESULT
  @@RESULT-BEGIN@@
  (filled in by bin/choupo-curate after the run)
  @@RESULT-END@@
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

operations
(
    {
        name       fit_antoine;
        type       vaporPressureFit;
        component  diEthylCarbonate;

        evidence
        (
            {
                dataset   "constant/archiveExtracts/diEthylCarbonate-vapourPressure-j.jct.2008.02.012.dat";
                identity  { doi "10.1016/j.jct.2008.02.012"; }
                role      fit;
            }
            {
                dataset   "constant/archiveExtracts/diEthylCarbonate-vapourPressure-acs.jced.7b00295.dat";
                identity  { doi "10.1021/acs.jced.7b00295"; }
                role      validation;
            }
        );

        acceptance
        {
            maxAAD  2.0 percent;
            origin  "declared before the fit by bin/choupo-curate vp (C281 step 2): the held-out study's own stated relative expanded uncertainty U95(P)/P, AVERAGED over its 42 points (1.29 to 3.99 %, mean 1.947 %), rounded UP to two significant figures -- a mean held against the held-out AAD, which is a mean";
        }

        output     { file fit_antoine.csv; }
    }
);
